==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[horse-fly]]
* [[horse fly]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|horse fliȝe}}, equivalent to {{af|en|horse|fly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-us-horsefly.ogg|audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several medium to large [[flies]], of the [[family]] [[Tabanidae]], that suck the [[blood]] of [[mammal]]s (not to be confused with {{taxlink|Stomoxys calcitrans|species}}, the [[stable fly]], or {{vern|dog fly}}).
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2017|author=Neil Gaiman|authorlink=Neil Gaiman|publisher=Bloomsbury Publishing|title=Norse Mythology|page=36|passage=It was not a '''horsefly''' and it was not a deerfly; it was bigger than either.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|fly of family Tabanidae}} {{l|en|cleg}} {{qualifier|dialectal}}, [[breezefly]], [[gadfly]], {{l|en|stoat-fly}}, {{l|en|stout}}

====Hyponyms====
* {{sense|individual species or subgroups of the family Tabanidae}} {{l|en|deer fly}}, {{l|en|Wikipedia:Deer fly|yellow fly}}, {{l|en|March fly}} {{qualifier|Australia}}, [[zimb]]

